vyweight (≤94 kg), Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "13 August 2016 — 15:30 (B) (A)"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/924"} "Riocentro Pavilhão 2, Parque Olímpico da Barra, Barra da Tijuca, Rio de Janeiro"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/354335"} "18 from 15 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Total of best lifts in snatch and clean &amp; jerk determined placement.  Ties broken by lightest bodyweight."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The landscape on this field changed days before the Rio Olympics, after 2012 85 kg Olympic champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/121168"} "Adrian Zieliński"] " of Poland, and his brother " [:a {:href "/athletes/121171"} "Tomasz"] " both failed drug tests. Also missing was the former 2012 Olympic champion, and current world record holder, " [:a {:href "/athletes/116393"} "Ilya Ilyin"] " of Kazakhstan, who had failed retests of his doping samples from the 2008 and 2012 Olympics, and had his results annulled, and medals stripped."] "\n\n" [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/116389"} "Vadim Streltsov"] " of Belarus, the 2015 World champion, looked to have the distinct advantage in the clean &amp; jerk going into Rio. Meanwhile, " [:a {:href "/athletes/135060"} "Aurimas Didžbalis"] ", who became the first Lithuanian to win a medal in the total weight at the World Championships, with bronze in 2014, was also in the reckoning. However, he had a poor showing at the 2015 Worlds, and missed the 2012 Olympic Games due to a doping suspension, so he was looking for some redemption. The dark horse was 2012 Olympian " [:a {:href "/athletes/124466"} "Sohrab Moradi"] " of Iran, who had totalled 400 kg at the Fajr Cup in Tehran earlier in the year."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Morabi took a healthy lead of 5 kg into the clean &amp; jerk, following a snatch of 182 kg, His first lift in the clean &amp; jerk of 221 kg, gave him a total of 403 kg sand secured the gold medal, and his country’s second weightlifting gold in as many nights."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Streltsov earned the silver with a total of 395 kg. Even though he missed his final lift Didžbalis was guaranteed the bronze medal, Lithuania’s first weightlifting medal ever, and he celebrated by doing a back flip."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Kilograms"] [:th {} "Bodyweight"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/124466"} "Sohrab Moradi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/IRI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/IRI.png"}] "IRI"]] [:td {} "403"] [:td {} "93.64"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/116389"} "Vadzim Straltsou"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BLR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BLR.png"}] "BLR"]] [:td {} "395"] [:td {} "93.70"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/135060"} "Aurimas Didžbalis"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/LTU"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/LTU.png"}] "LTU"]] [:td {} "392"] [:td {} "92.42"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:class "footnote", :href "#", :title "Doping positive announced in January 2026 by the ITA after re-test revealed presence of methandienone (Dianabol) metabolite. Medal status pending as of 25 Jan 2026.", :data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right"} "1"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td 